Linux Operations Lab
This is my hands-on Linux practice lab.
I am using Ubuntu to practice basic Linux commands, networking, system monitoring, troubleshooting, and other operations-related tasks.

Network Commands:

1. Check IP Address
   Command:
       ip address
   What it does:
       Shows the network interfaces and the IP addresses assigned to them.
   What I learned:
       lo is the loopback interface.
       wlp2s0 is my Wi-Fi interface.
       The inet value shows the IP address.

2. Check Network Interfaces
   Command:
       ip link
   What it does:
       Shows the available network interfaces and their status.
   What I learned:
       UP means the interface is enabled.
       LOWER_UP means the network link is active.
       lo is the loopback interface.

4. Check Routing
   Command:
        ip route
   What it does:
        Shows how Linux routes network traffic.
   What I learned:
        default via shows the default gateway.
        dev shows the network interface used for the route.

4. Test Network Connectivity
   Command:
        ping 8.8.8.8
   What it does:
        Tests whether my system can reach the IP address 8.8.8.8.
   What I learned:
        ping uses ICMP to check network connectivity. If I receive replies, the destination is reachable.

Note:
   I am learning these commands by running them on my Ubuntu system, checking the output, and documenting what I understand from each command.
